Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: ingenic: x1600: use the TCU watchdog clock

The watchdog driver requests the lowest available clock rate to fit its
timeout into the 16-bit counter. Passing the fixed 32768 Hz RTC clock
directly bypasses the TCU prescaler and limits max_timeout to one second.
This leaves no margin for a userspace feeder running once per second.

Use the TCU watchdog clock so clk_set_rate() programs the hardware
prescaler and the driver calculates the timeout from the divided rate.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/x1600.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/x1600.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/x1600.dtsi
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/x1600.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/x1600.dtsi
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@
 				compatible = "ingenic,x1600-watchdog", "ingenic,jz4780-watchdog";
 				reg = <0 0x10>;
 
-				clocks = <&cgu X1600_CLK_RTCLK>;
+				clocks = <&tcu TCU_CLK_WDT>;
 				clock-names = "wdt";
 
 			// data sheet mentiones a "half interrupt"
